## Chapter 26: The Deep Grinding Grounds
The lowest drainage tier of Sub-Level 4 was an uncharted labyrinth of flooded concrete tunnels and subterranean runoff channels.
While Renna, Tobias, and Mina held a choke-point near the primary drainage valve—using Renna’s tower shield to funnel low-tier stragglers into Tobias’s crossbow line—Kaelen took advantage of the thick purple mist and zero drone coverage.
"I'll secure the side overflow channel," Kaelen stammered meekly, lowering his hood and clutching his dented iron pipe. "I'll lay wire traps so nothing sneaks up from behind us."
"Don't go past twenty meters, Kaelen," Renna called out over the sound of her shield absorbing a impact. "Call out if you see anything heavy!"
"Got it, Renna!"
The second Kaelen stepped around the flooded concrete bend, out of sight of his team, his slouched posture disappeared. His eyes sharpened into a cold, predatory focus as he engaged **[Shadow-Veil Cloak]**, his body blending seamlessly into the dark mist.
*Time to clear the sector.*
His **[Hive-Mind Synapse]** mapped the cavern ahead. A massive nest of **Grave-Spite Crawlers (Tier-D Elite)** and two **Abyssal Carapace Behemoths (Tier-C)** were guarding a deep flooded reservoir.
Kaelen didn't hesitate.
*SHHH!*
He triggered **[Void-Step]**, phase-shifting fifteen meters in a microsecond and appearing directly in the center of the nesting chamber.
The fifteen Grave-Spite Crawlers hissed, their barbed tails whipping forward in a rain of toxic needles.
Moving at his base **68 Agility**, Kaelen didn't even need to trigger [Kinetic Overdrive]. He wove through the projectile rain like a phantom.
 * *PUNCH.* His **67 Strength**, backed by the 15% kinetic amplification of his custom **Kinetic-Void Bracers**, shattered the first Crawler’s skull into dust.
 * *STEP.* He pivoted on his heel, using his **Anchor-Greaves** to drive a low side-kick into the second beast's knee joint, snapping the leg and sending it crashing into two others.
 * *GRAB & CRUSH.* He caught a leaping Crawler by its throat with his left hand, squeezing until the chitin armor buckled, and slammed its body into the stone floor.
Three seconds. Four dead.
The two **Abyssal Carapace Behemoths (Tier-C)**—twelve-foot armored quadrupeds with heavy, stone-hard skull plates—roared, charging him simultaneously from opposite sides to crush him between their massive frames.
Kaelen stood his ground, planting both feet with the absolute weight of his **[Terrestrial Anchor]**.
"**[Kinetic Overdrive]**!"
A dark wave of kinetic energy surged through his nervous system.
Kaelen ducked under the left Behemoth's crushing jaw, drove an open-palm strike straight up into its lower jaw seam, and used his raw **67 Strength** to flip the five-ton beast clean over his shoulder, slamming it directly into the second charging Behemoth.
*BOOOOOOM!*
The concussive impact echoed through the subterranean chamber like an artillery detonation.
Before the two dazed Tier-C beasts could recover, Kaelen phase-shifted above them with **[Void-Step]**. He closed both fists, driving a double downward strike straight into their cracked skull seams.
*CRACK-BOOM!*
Both Tier-C Behemoths went limp, their vital cores shattered instantly.
Kaelen landed lightly on his feet, deactivating his skills as he slammed both bare palms onto the massive carcasses.
"**[Dissect & Assimilate]**!"
Dark gray vapor erupted from his hands, devouring the two Behemoths and the remaining eleven Crawlers in a violent, silent vortex.
